# What the static site Worker "guzzionboard" must never publish.
#
# Read by wrangler when it uploads assets (see wrangler.jsonc, which pins the
# asset directory to the repository root). Two jobs:
#
#   1. keep build output, caches and local tooling out of the public site - the
#      build container runs `pip install .` before deploying, so build/,
#      *.egg-info/ and caches exist there even though git ignores them;
#   2. keep the research binaries out of the CDN. The repository root carries
#      OEM calibration archives and flash dumps (7SM_*, MIUG3_*, 5AM_*,
#      Hayabusa gen 3 stock.bin and others) plus byte-identical copies under
#      docs/. None of them is linked from any page, none is licensed by this
#      project, and a branded calibration file is not covered by the repository
#      licence - see docs/DYNOAI_AND_UPLOADS.md. They stay in git and on
#      GitHub; they are simply not served from this site.
#
# A single file of 25 MiB or more in an unignored directory fails the whole
# deploy ("Asset too large"), which is why node_modules/ is listed explicitly:
# it contains a 137 MiB workerd binary.

# Version control and the build configuration itself.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.assetsignore

# Local environments and dependencies.
node_modules
.venv
venv
.wrangler
.wrangler-dryrun
.dev.vars*

# Build output and caches.
build
dist
*.egg-info
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
coverage
captures
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.desktop-test-data
packaging/windows_version_info.txt
packaging/resources/*.exe

# Research binaries: third-party calibration archives, never served.
*.bin
*.zip
*.jsonl
